Don't really know if my problem is exactly the same for everyone. I wasn't able to connect internally to rke2 services with cilium on nixOs participant2 firewall. What I did is disable participant2 firewall and use nftables.

```nix
  networking = {
    nftables.enable = true;
    firewall = {
      enable = lib.mkForce false;
    };
  };
```

Cons is that we have to open ports with our own nft rules.

@participant20 
in my case all cilium related interfaces must be trusted, because in nixos e.g. nftables is evaluated first. My guess is that trusting them on your side will allow you to use the firewall again.

Important is the glob. This is nftables specific. For iptables it would be a '+'? (I forgot the correct wildcard.. :)

```nix
  networking = {
    firewall = {
      checkReversePath = "loose";
      interfaces.eno1 = {
        allowedTCPPorts = [
          22
          8080
        ];
      };
      trustedInterfaces = [
        "cilium_host"
        "cilium_net"
        "cilium_vxlan"
        "lxc*"
      ];
    };
  };
```

